🚨 Incident Response Planning for a Ransomware Attack
Overview

This project presents a comprehensive Incident Response (IR), Business Continuity (BC), and Recovery Strategy for a fictional ransomware incident affecting Northbridge Skills Institute. The exercise evaluates incident classification, response coordination, evidence preservation, communication planning, recovery procedures, and post-incident improvements aligned with cybersecurity governance and industry best practices.

Scenario Summary

At 08:45 WAT, Northbridge Skills Institute detected a critical cybersecurity incident involving:

Confirmed ransomware activity on FIN-PC07 and FS01
Loss of access to learning materials and student assessments
Suspicious privileged account activity
Unusual outbound data transfer of approximately 1.2 GB
Potential compromise of backup infrastructure
An upcoming online examination scheduled for 11:00 WAT

The primary objectives were:

Contain the threat.
Preserve forensic evidence.
Protect backup systems.
Maintain business continuity.
Safely restore services.
Determine whether data exfiltration occurred.
